  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Glyceryl monostearate may interact with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through a series of intermediate targets. The compound is implicated in targeting Peptide deformylase, which in turn is a target of Sugiol and Cinnabaramide C, all of which ultimately lead to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. This indicates a potential pathway where Glyceryl monostearate may influence the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 via the modulation of its downstream targets. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence highlights the importance of Peptide deformylase as a key mediator in this pathway, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between Glyceryl monostearate and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4.",
